# HTML Structure Rules - Next.js App Router

## CRITICAL: Document-Level Tag Restrictions

### ✅ ALLOWED Locations for `<html>` and `<body>`

**ONLY these files may contain `<html>` or `<body>` tags:**

1. `app/layout.tsx` (root layout) - **REQUIRED**
   - Must contain both `<html>` and `<body>`
   - Structure: `<html>` → `<body>` → providers → `{children}`

2. `app/global-error.tsx` (global error boundary) - **OPTIONAL**
   - May contain `<html>` and `<body>` (replaces root layout on critical errors)
   - Only used when root layout fails to render

### ❌ FORBIDDEN Locations for `<html>` or `<body>`

**NEVER render `<html>`, `<body>`, or `<head>` in:**

- `app/**/page.tsx` (any page component)
- `app/**/layout.tsx` (nested layouts)
- `app/**/error.tsx` (route-level error boundaries)
- `app/**/template.tsx` (templates)
- `components/**` (any component file)
- `app/**/*.tsx` (any other app file)

### ❌ FORBIDDEN Patterns

```tsx
// ❌ NEVER in nested layouts
export default function NestedLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html>  {/* FORBIDDEN */}
      <body> {/* FORBIDDEN */}
        {children}
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}

// ❌ NEVER in pages
export default function Page() {
  return (
    <html>  {/* FORBIDDEN */}
      <body> {/* FORBIDDEN */}
        <div>Content</div>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}

// ❌ NEVER in error boundaries (except global-error.tsx)
export default function Error({ error, reset }) {
  return (
    <html>  {/* FORBIDDEN */}
      <body> {/* FORBIDDEN */}
        <div>Error</div>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}

// ❌ NEVER in components
export function MyComponent() {
  return (
    <html>  {/* FORBIDDEN */}
      <body> {/* FORBIDDEN */}
        <div>Content</div>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

### ✅ CORRECT Patterns

```tsx
// ✅ Root layout (app/layout.tsx)
export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <ThemeProvider>
          {children}
        </ThemeProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}

// ✅ Nested layout (app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx)
export default function DashboardLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <div className="dashboard">
      <Sidebar />
      <main>{children}</main>
    </div>
  );
}

// ✅ Page (app/page.tsx)
export default function HomePage() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Home</h1>
    </div>
  );
}

// ✅ Error boundary (app/error.tsx)
export default function Error({ error, reset }) {
  return (
    <div className="error-container">
      <h1>Error</h1>
      <button onClick={reset}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Enforcement Rules

1. **Before creating any file in `app/` or `components/`:**
   - Verify it does NOT contain `<html>`, `<body>`, or `<head>` tags
   - Use semantic HTML containers instead (`<div>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, etc.)

2. **When modifying `app/layout.tsx`:**
   - Ensure `<html>` directly wraps `<body>`
   - Ensure `<body>` directly wraps providers and `{children}`
   - Do NOT add intermediate wrappers

3. **When creating error boundaries:**
   - `app/error.tsx` → NO `<html>`/`<body>` (returns content only)
   - `app/global-error.tsx` → MAY have `<html>`/`<body>` (replaces root layout)

4. **suppressHydrationWarning:**
   - Only use on `<html>` if theme provider causes class mismatches
   - Do NOT use on `<body>` unless absolutely necessary
   - Prefer fixing the root cause over suppressing warnings

## Why These Rules Exist

- **Hydration Errors**: Invalid HTML structure causes React hydration mismatches
- **Next.js Architecture**: App Router handles document structure automatically
- **Performance**: Extra document tags break Next.js optimizations
- **Maintainability**: Clear rules prevent future bugs

## Quick Check

Before committing any file:

```bash
# Check for forbidden tags
grep -r "<html\|</html>\|<body\|</body>" app/ components/ --include="*.tsx" | grep -v "layout.tsx\|global-error.tsx\|HTMLFormElement\|HTMLInputElement"
```

If this command returns any results (excluding `layout.tsx` and `global-error.tsx`), **fix the violation before committing**.

